=== NOTE on timing anomaly ===
First JDK19 run (tracePinnedThreads, no JFR) printed only ONE pinned-stack dump (not 100) and finished in 5195ms, not the naive 10000ms.
This is because the FJP-based virtual-thread scheduler compensates for a pinned/blocked carrier by spawning extra carrier OS threads even with parallelism=1,
so the 100 sequential 100ms pins do not fully serialize on one carrier, and tracePinnedThreads output for repeated identical call sites appears to be deduplicated by the JVM.
The JFR-recording run of the same code (command [2]) instead completed in 10352ms and recorded exactly 100 jdk.VirtualThreadPinned events — matching the naive expectation.
Both program runs are real; both output blocks above are kept verbatim.
